  },
  {
    "episode_id": 84654,
    "turn_file": "/shared/3/projects/podcasts/transcriptionQueue/turns/pol_appearance_episodes_interviews/8/4/84654.jsonl",
    "turn_idx": 11,
    "turn_text": "So I want to start by saying I didn't do anything. It was a team that we were able to build from the very beginning You know, we launched on June 18, 2019 with the endorsement of the Justice Democrats. We were their first endorsement in New York since AOC. So it was huge to come out of the gate with that level of support. And across the duration of the campaign, we were endorsed by 60 individuals in grassroots organizations. And we were able to build a diverse coalition to really connect with all parts of the district building strong, deep, authentic relationships. And we started early and often by knocking on the doors of people who one may think are not the consistent voters, people who have been historically neglected. And because of that, they historically been disengaged. So we started early and often to connect with them. And we wanted them to know that they were not just a part of this race and helping us get to victory. But we wanted them to be a part of our democracy going forward. And we wanted their voices to be centered as we draft policy in Washington. So that's what it was. We had an amazing team, a diverse coalition. We connected with voters who had been ignored for quite some time. And that's how we were able to pull out the win.",
