    "turn_text": "You know, that's a great question. You know, so what I want to say about that is, you know, people who are white and wealthy care about racial and economic justice as well. I think that's a misperception that they don't. So, you know, when we are connected with people in those communities, we continue to send a racial and economic justice through the lens of environmental justice, fully funding our public schools, universal health care, a green new deal, and a federal jobs guarantee. So the people in those areas care about those issues as well, while the people in the North Bronx, as well as Yonkers Mount Vernon, New Rochelle, who are actually living with those issues, living with the issues of racial injustice and economic injustice on a day-to-day basis. So that's what our campaign was all about, and that's why we were able to pull people in from across the district. And again, as I mentioned, the diverse coalitions, we have volunteers and supporters of our campaign from every town and every part of the district. So that was also very helpful. And",
