    "turn_text": "You know, we tried reconstruction after the Civil War. Unfortunately, Abraham Lincoln was murdered and a racist took over as president and he took our 40 acres away from us and gave it to the Confederate rebels who were traitors of our country at that time. He also allowed the Homestead Act to give hundreds of thousands, millions of acres actually to white settlers, both native born and foreign born. And none of that capital was provided to recently free slaves. So we were freed, but we were left homeless right after that freedom. The second reconstruction was attempted after the Civil Rights Movement. And unfortunately, at the same time, there was a war on drugs, quote unquote, and mass incarceration ensued. For this reconstruction, our reconstruction agenda is focusing on police brutality, mass incarceration, but also institutional racism in all its forms. And it includes a period of truth and reconciliation similar to what happened in Rwanda, South Africa and Germany, which will allow us to finally reckon with our history as a country and reckon with the legacy of slavery and racism. In our country, it includes reparations and massive investment in black and brown communities. And it includes shift from the overmilitarization and over-policing of communities towards a new vision, a holistic vision of public safety and public health. So investing more in housing and food and education and healthcare and environmental justice. a jobs guarantee and mental health supports. That's what provides true safety and security, not over policing and over militarization.",
