    "turn_file": "/shared/3/projects/podcasts/transcriptionQueue/turns/pol_appearance_episodes_interviews/8/4/84654.jsonl",
    "turn_idx": 30,
    "turn_text": "And you mentioned the election, of course, in November. I just want to make a quick note that you are actually running on a post. There is no Republican opponent in your race. So you are basically in there right now. You're going to be starting in next year, in January, 2021. Speaking of the election, I have to talk about it in November. Again, you don't have to run because, again, you're running on a post, but the president does, he has to be run again for reelection. There's a very interesting movement going on right now. We've seen it in our streets. We're seeing it in the media. We're seeing it even in corporate America and to some extent. Do you think that with everything that's going on right now that Trump can be defeated in November?",
